# What this module needs that no single spoon owns.
#
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason, the same five fields a spoon uses. The
# collector stamps the consumer column with this module's name, since the need belongs to the
# module as a whole rather than to anything inside it.
#
# Nothing here is read by the running config. The resolver inside .hammerspoon serves plugins and
# probes only what a plugin declared, so a need like the application itself, which has no runtime
# consumer because nothing would be running without it, is declared here instead.
#
# Named dependencies-module rather than dependencies because this directory already holds the
# generated DEPENDENCIES, and on a case insensitive filesystem those two names are one file.
hammerspoon | app | org.hammerspoon.Hammerspoon | required | the application this entire module configures

# The collector beside this file reads every plugin's manifest to build the generated
# DEPENDENCIES, and those manifests are written in Lua, so reading them takes Lua. Optional
# rather than required, because the running configuration does not care. Only regenerating this
# module's contract with the layer above stops working, which is a maintenance task rather than
# a feature, and the reconciler above says so plainly when it cannot run.
lua | path | lua | optional | reading every plugin manifest so the collector can build this module's generated manifest
